Hey, my name is Dana.

In February 2018 I quit my job in San Francisco and <%= link_to 'moved into a campervan', '/tags/van' %> full-time. I spent about a year traveling the US, and shared photos and stories from the road here on this site. A dashcam rode along the whole way.

The van is long gone. The footage isn't. It became <%= link_to 'A Dana Life', 'https://www.twitch.tv/ADanaLife_' %>, a 24/7 slow-tv stream: dashcam footage of American roads, landscapes and small towns, playing around the clock. A chatbot lets viewers check where the van is, guess what state it's in, and earn miles for watching.

The stream went dark in 2021. In 2026 I rebuilt it from the ground up and turned it back on. It plays on Twitch and YouTube, and it is still the most boring stream on Twitch.

The same footage runs <%= link_to 'Guessr', 'https://guessr.dana.lol' %>, a game where you watch three seconds of the drive and guess where in the country it was filmed. It's on the web and the App Store.

To find me on social media, please visit the <%= link_to('contact page', '/contact') %>.

If you're looking to hire me, <%= link_to('my resume is available on Github', 'https://github.com/dmerrick/resume') %>.

If you're looking for more info on how I built this site, the source code is available on Github <%= link_to('here', 'https://github.com/adanalife/website') %>, and I have written two blog articles explaining my process: <%= link_to('part 1', '/2017/10/01/how-this-site-works/') %> and <%= link_to('part 2', '/2017/10/12/how-this-site-works-p-2/') %>.
